sec.p:
Data were analyzed using Review Manager 5.3 and TSA 0.9.5.10 Beta program. We presented results as forest plots through the risk ratios (RRs) with 95% confidence intervals (CI) for dichotomous data. Forest plots using the mean difference (MD) with 95% CI were performed for continuous data. The heterogeneity was defined via I2 statistic. An I2-value > 50% was considered heterogeneity. Random-effects model was used for all pooled analysis. If the value of P was less than 0.05, regarded as statistically significant. We also conducted a TSA to control random errors and calculate the required information size (RIS) based on a two-sided \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
